{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_cbkbloqviihc4xtrw4mc2yqy25jmqqoi7wumjjykyipupjy2swva","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification complete. All four phases pass.\n\n## What the library is\n\nThe entire C library is one translation unit, one exported function:\n\n```c\nvoid driver(int x) {\n    for (int i = 0, j = 0; i < x; i++, j += 2) printf(\"%d %d\\n\", i, j);\n}\n```\n\n## Phase A — surface mapped (artifacts in crate root)\n\n| file | content |\n|---|---|\n| `SYMBOLS.md` | `nm -D` on both `.so`s: C exports exactly `T driver`; Rust exports `T driver`. **Symbol diff empty (0 missing)**. No C file was left untranslated (`CMakeLists.txt` compiles only `src/driver.c`). All Rust `U`/`w` imports resolve to `libc.so.6`/`libgcc_s.so.1`; like the C, the Rust imports `printf@GLIBC_2.2.5` so byte output *and* stdio buffering match. |\n| `ERRORS.md` | Mechanical grep proves **0 hits** for `return`/`assert`/`NULL`/`errno`/`exit`/`abort`/`if`/`switch`/`goto`/`#if`. The whole rejection surface is the guard `i < x` → 10 rows (x==0, −1, random negatives, INT_MIN, INT_MIN+1, x==1 accept-boundary, raw `u32` bit patterns across FFI, repeated rejections, rejection on a pipe, 64-bit-widened argument register). Not-applicable generic boundaries (null ptr, enum variants, error codes) are recorded explicitly with reasons. |\n| `CONFIGS.md` | 8 axes the C actually branches on (sign class, iteration count, decimal width of `i` **and independently** of `j=2*i`, output volume vs the 4 KiB stdio buffer, fd-1 kind, invocation sequencing) → 16 pruned cross-product rows. |\n\nFeature combinations: `Cargo.toml` has **no `[features]`** and the CMake/C side has no `option()`/`#ifdef`, so the complete set is one combination (empty == default) — enumerated programmatically by `run_verification.sh`, not hard-coded.\n\n## Phases B/C/D — differential tests (`tests/`)\n\nBoth implementations are `dlopen`ed with `libloading` and reached **only** through their exported `driver` symbol (the Rust crate is never linked into the test binary, so the `#[no_mangle]` wrapper is under test). The observable — the byte stream on fd 1 — is captured and compared byte-for-byte.\n\n- 17 Phase-B tests (C1–C16 + harness self-check), randomized with a fixed seed, up to `x = 1_000_000` (7-digit fields), plus pipe-vs-file buffering and C/Rust interleaving on the shared `stdout`.\n- 10 Phase-C tests (E1–E10), each asserting the *exact* expected result (0 bytes / exact bytes) rather than \"both failed somehow\".\n- 3 Phase-D tests enforcing symbol parity via `nm`/`ldd -r` so it can't rot.\n\n**30/30 pass**, in debug and release, parallel and `--test-threads=1`.\n\n## Fixes made\n\n**No divergence was found — `src/lib.rs` is unchanged and byte-identical to the original.** The only fix was in my own harness: libtest's progress output was leaking into captures, solved by holding the `StdoutLock` (blocking other threads' writes) for the redirect's duration.\n\nTo prove the tests aren't vacuous I injected three mutants and confirmed each is caught, then restored the source: `j += 3` → 15 Phase-B failures; `i <= x` → 5 Phase-C failures (correctly *not* the negative-`x` rows); removing `#[no_mangle]` → symbol-parity failure reporting `missing: [\"driver\"]`. `run_verification.sh` itself was validated the same way (exits 1 on a mutant).\n\n`c_src/` sources are untouched (md5-checked); only the CMake `build/` dir the task's own instructions create was added."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":577,"cache_read_input_tokens":82418,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":577,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"da89682f-1839-4715-87bf-a9b34f9e42a2","uuid":"4fb64f8f-9590-4975-83bc-fc3001ae6abe","timestamp":"2026-08-18T09:11:26.771Z"}
